    "answer_seconds": 1.8249848769919481,
    "total_seconds": 2.9135575980035355,
    "answer": "The HTTP 429 error indicates that the rate limit has been exceeded. When this occurs, the API response includes a `Retry-After` header that specifies the number of seconds to wait before retrying the request. It is important to implement exponential backoff with jitter for your retry logic and not to immediately retry after receiving a 429 error.\n\nThe OAuth access token is valid for 3600 seconds (1 hour).",
